        window.__PRELOADED_STATE__ = {"abstracts":{"content":[{"$$":[{"$":{"id":"d1e2525"},"#name":"section-title","_":"Abstract"},{"$$":[{"$$":[{"#name":"text","$$":[{"#name":"__text__","_":"The extensive computational burden limits the usage of "},{"#name":"topic-link","_":"convolutional neural networks","$":{"href":"/topics/computer-science/convolutional-neural-network","term":"convolutional neural networks"}},{"#name":"text","$$":[{"#name":"text","$$":[{"#name":"__text__","_":" (CNNs) in edge devices for image "},{"#name":"topic-link","_":"semantic segmentation","$":{"href":"/topics/computer-science/image-segmentation","term":"semantic segmentation"}},{"#name":"__text__","_":", which plays a significant role in many real-world applications, such as "}]},{"#name":"topic-link","_":"augmented reality","$":{"href":"/topics/engineering/augmented-reality","term":"augmented reality"}},{"#name":"__text__","_":", robotics, and self-driving. To address this problem, this paper presents an attention-guided lightweight network, namely "}]}]},{"#name":"italic","_":"AGLNet"},{"#name":"text","$$":[{"#name":"__text__","_":", which employs an encoder–decoder architecture for real-time semantic segmentation. Specifically, the encoder adopts a novel residual module to abstract feature representations, where two new operations, channel split and shuffle, are utilized to greatly reduce computation cost while maintaining higher "},{"#name":"topic-link","_":"segmentation accuracy","$":{"href":"/topics/computer-science/segmentation-accuracy","term":"segmentation accuracy"}},{"#name":"text","$$":[{"#name":"__text__","_":". On the other hand, instead of using complicated dilated convolution and artificially designed architecture, two types of "},{"#name":"topic-link","_":"attention mechanism","$":{"href":"/topics/computer-science/attention-machine-learning","term":"attention mechanism"}},{"#name":"text","$$":[{"#name":"__text__","_":" are subsequently employed in the decoder to upsample 