 (LAEDNet), for automatic ultrasound image segmentation. In contrast to previous encoder–decoder networks that involve complicated architecture with numerous parameters, our LAEDNet adopts lightweight version of EfficientNet as encoder. On the other hand, a Lightweight Residual Squeeze-and-Excitation (LRSE) block is employed in decoder. To achieve trade-off between segmentation accuracy and implementing efficiency, we also present a family of models, from light to heavy (denoted as LAEDNet-S, LAEDNet-M, and LAEDNet-L, respectively), with varying lightweight version of EfficientNet backbones. To evaluate LAEDNet, we have conducted extensive experiments on Brachial Plexus Dataset (BP), Breast Ultrasound Images Dataset (BUSI), and Head Circumference Ultrasound Images Dataset (HCUS), where ultrasound images are suffered from high noise, blurred borders and low contrast. The experiments show that, compared with U-Net and its variants, e.g., M-Net, U-Net++ and TransUNet, our LAEDNet achieves better results in terms of Dice Coefficient (DSC) and running speed. Particularly, LAEDNet-M only has 10.75M model parameters with 40.7 FPS, yet obtaining 73.0%, 73.8% and 91.3% DSC on BP, BUSI and HCUS datasets, respectively."}],"$":{"view":"all","id":"d1e2606"},"#name":"abstract-sec"}],"$":{"view":"all","id":"d1e2603","class":"author"},"#name":"abstract"},{"$$":[{"$":{"id":"d1e2610"},"#name":"section-title","_":"Highlights"},{"$$":[{"$$":[{"$$":[{"$$":[{"#name":"label","_":"•"},{"$":{"view":"all","id":"d1e2619"},"#name":"para","_":"We design a Lightweight Attention Encoder–Decoder Network (LAEDNet) for ultrasound medical image segmentation."}],"$":{"id":"d1e2616"},"#name":"list-item"},{"$$":[{"#name":"label","_":"•"},{"$":{"view":"all","id":"d1e2624"},"#name":"para","_":"With the guidance of visual attention, a LRSE block is designed to coupled with LAEDNet backbone."}],"$":{"id":"d1e2621"},"#name":"list-item"},{"$$":[{"#name":"label","_":"•"},{"$":{"view":"all","id":"d1e2629"},"#name":"para","_":"LAEDNet achieves best trade-off of accuracy and efficiency on 3 ultrasound medical image datasets"}],"$":{"id":"d1e2626"},"#name":"list-item"}],"$":{"id":"d1e2615"},"#name":"list"}],"$":{"view":"all","id":"d1e2613"},"#name":"simple-para"}],"$":{"view":"all","id":"d1e2612"},"#name":"abstract-sec"}],"$":{"view":"all","id":"d1e2609","class":"author-highlights"},"#name":"abstract"}],"$":{"xmlns:ce":true,"xmlns:dm":true,"xmlns:sb":true},"#name":"abstracts"}},{"articleTitle":"CS-ResNet: Cost-sensitive residual convolutional neural network for PCB cosmetic defect detection","authors":"Zhang H., Jiang L., Li C.","doi":"10.1016/j.eswa.2021.115673","externalArticle":false,"issn":"09574174","openAccess":0,"pii":"S0957417421010617","publicationDate":"2021-12-15","publicationTitle":"Expert Systems with Applications","publicationYear":"2021","scopusArticleUrl":"http://www.scopus.com/scopus/inward/record.url?partnerID=10&rel=3.0.0&view=basic&eid=2-s2.0-85111598390&md5=f82ac77a979a751c186ca6983c9b25c","scopusEid":"2-s2.0-85111598390","thirdParty":false,"volume":"Volume 185","abstract":{"$$":[{"$$":[{"$$":[{"#name":"attachment-eid","_":"1-s2.0-S0957417421010617-si1.svg"},{"#name":"ucs-locator","_":"https://s3-eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/prod-ucs-content-store-eu-west/content/pii:S0957417421010617/STRIPIN/image/svg+xml/076672e25b7bca63deeffee58e506b05/si1.svg"},{"#name":"file-basename","_":"si1"},{"#name":"abstract-attachment","_":"true"},{"#name":"filename","_":"si1.svg"},{"#name":"extension","_":"svg"},{"#name":"filesize","_":"8299"},{"#name":"attachment-type","_":"ALTIMG"}],"$":{"xmlns:xocs":true},"#name":"attachment"},{"$$":[{"#name":"attachment-eid","_":"1-s2.0-S0957417421010617-si2.svg"},{"#name":"ucs-locator","_":"https://s3-eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/prod-ucs-content-store-eu-west/content/pii:S0957417421010617/STRIPIN/image/svg+xml/53a74070ce6d9cb12d7926f8f9d5669d/si2.svg"},{"#name":"file-basename","_":"si2"},{"#name":"abstract-attachment","_":"true"},{"#name":"filename","_":"si2.svg"},{"#name":"extension","_":"svg"},{"#name":"filesize","_":"1462"},{"#name":"attachment-type","_":"ALTIMG"}],"$":{"xmlns:xocs":true},"#name":"attachment"},{"$$":[{"#name":"attachment-eid","_":"1-s2.0-S0957417421010617-si3.svg"},{"#name":"ucs-locator","_":"https://s3-eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/prod-ucs-content-store-eu-west/content/pii:S0957417421010617/STRIPIN/image/svg+xml/7d7d5186353fc674e8ce2039c58c7a56/si3.svg"},{"#name":"file-basename","_":"si3"},{"#name":"abstract-attachment","_":"true"},{"#name":"filename","_":"si3.svg"},{"#name":"extension","_":"svg"},{"#name":"filesize","_":"5078"},{"#name":"attachment-type","_":"ALTIMG"}],"$":{"xmlns:xocs":true},"#name":"attachment"}],"#name":"attachments"},{"$$":[{"$":{"id":"d1e828"},"#name":"section-title","_":"Abstract"},{"$$":[{"$$":[{"#name":"__text__","_":"In the printed circuit board (PCB) industry, cosmetic defect detection is an essential process to ensure product quality. However, existing PCB cosmetic defect detection approaches have a high false alarm rate, which lead to expensive labor costs of manual confirmation. To solve this problem, some traditional machine learning-based approaches have been proposed, but they just utilize hand-crafted features to build classifiers and thus are rough and sub-optimal. Recently, due to its powerful capability in automatic feature extraction, convolutional neural network (CNN) has been widely used in PCB cosmetic defect detection. However, few of them pay attention to the imbalanced class distribution as well as the different misclassification costs of real and pseudo defects, both of which are common problems in the PCB industry. To this end, in this study, we propose a novel model called cost-sensitive residual convolutional neural network (CS-ResNet) by adding a cost-sensitive adjustment layer in the standard ResNet. Specifically, we assign larger weights to minority real defects based on the class-imbalance degree and then optimize CS-ResNet by minimizing the weighted cross-entropy loss function. We conducted a series of experiments by comparing CS-ResNet with the standard ResNet, state-of-the-art CNN-based approach Auto-VRS and traditional machine learning-based approach HOG-SVM on a real-world PCB cosmetic defect dataset. Experimental results show that CS-ResNet achieves the highest "},{"$$":[{"$$":[{"#name":"mi","_":"S"},{"#name":"mi","_":"e"},{"#name":"mi","_":"n"},{"#name":"mi","_":"s"},{"#name":"mi","_":"i"},{"#name":"mi","_":"t"},{"#name":"mi","_":"i"},{"#name":"mi","_":"v"},{"#name":"mi","_":"i"},{"#name":"mi","_":"t"},{"#name":"mi","_":"y"}],"#name":"mrow"}],"$":{"xmlns:mml":true,"altimg":"si1.svg","display":"inline","id":"d1e834"},"#name":"math"},{"#name":"__text__","_":" (0.89), "},{"$$":[{"#name":"mi","_":"G"}],"$":{"xmlns:mml":true,"altimg":"si2.svg","display":"inline","id":"d1e860"},"#name":"math"},{"#name":"__text__","_":"-"},{"$$":[{"$$":[{"#name":"mi","_":"m"},{"#name":"mi","_":"e"},{"#name":"mi","_":"a"},{"#name":"mi","_":"n"}],"#name":"mrow"}],"$":{"xmlns:mml":true,"altimg":"si3.svg","display":"inline","id":"d1e865"},"#name":"math"},{"#name":"__text__","_":" (0.91) and the lowest misclassification costs."}],"$":{"view":"all","id":"d1e831"},"#name":"simple-para"}],"$":{"view":"all","id":"d1e830"},"#name":"abstract-sec"}],"$":{"view":"all","id":"d1e827","class":"author"},"#name":"abstract"},{"$$":[{"$":{"id":"d1e877"},"#name":"section-title","_":"Highlights"},{"$$":[{"$$":[{"$$":[{"$$":[{"#name":"label","_":"•"},{"$":{"view":"all","id":"d1e886"},"#name":"para","_":"Cosmetic defect detection is an essential process in the PCB industry."}],"$":{"id":"d1e883"},"#name":"list-item"},{"$$":[{"#name":"label","_":"•"},{"$":{"view":"all","id":"d1e891"},"#name":"para","_":"We propose a cost-sensitive ResNet (CS-ResNet) for PCB cosmetic defect detection."}],"$":{"id":"d1e888"},"#name":"list-item"},{"$$":[{"#name":"label","_":"•"},{"$":{"view":"all","id":"d1e896"},"#name":"para","_":"In CS-ResNet, we add a cost-sensitive adjustment layer to optimize the CS-ResNet."}],"$":{"id":"d1e893"},"#name":"list-item"},{"$$":[{"#name":"label","_":"•"},{"$":{"view":"all","id":"d1e901"},"#name":"para","_":"Extensive empirical studies validate the effectiveness of the proposed CS-ResNet."}],"$":{"id":"d1e898"},"#name":"list-item"}],"$":{"id":"d1e882"},"#name":"list"}],"$":{"view":"all","id":"d1e880"},"#name":"simple-para"}],"$":{"view":"all","id":"d1e879"},"#name":"abstract-sec"}],"$":{"view":"all","id":"d1e876","class":"author-highlights"},"#name":"abstract"}],"$":{"xmlns:ce":true,"xmlns:dm":true,"xmlns:sb":true},"#name":"abstracts"}},{"articleTitle":"DSANet: Dilated spatial attention for real-time semantic segmentation in urban street scenes","authors":"Elhassan M.A.M., Huang C., Munea T.L.","doi":"10.1016/j.eswa.2021.115090","externalArticle":false,"issn":"09574174","openAccess":0,"pii":"S0957417421005315","publicationDate":"2021-11-30","publicationTitle":"Expert Systems with Applications","publicationYear":"2021","scopusArticleUrl":"http://www.scopus.com/scopus/inward/record.url?partnerID=10&rel=3.0.0&view=basic&eid=2-s2.0-85107733544&md5=7f8da8cdeb51d227f2c2a20bbf7401d","scopusEid":"2-s2.0-85107733544","thirdParty":false,"volume":"Volume 183","abstract":{"$$":[{"$$":[{"$":{"id":"st130"},"#name":"section-title","_":"Highlights"},{"$$":[{"$$":[{"$$":[{"$$":[{"#name":"label","_":"•"},{"$":{"view":"all","id":"p0230"},"#name":"para","_":"Real time semantic segmentation for road scene understanding."}],"$":{"id":"u0005"},"#name":"list-item"},{"$$":[{"#name":"label","_":"•"},{"$":{"view":"all","id":"p0235"},"#name":"para","_":"Follow two branch network strategy."}],"$":{"id":"u0010"},"#name":"list-item"},{"$$":[{"#name":"label","_":"•"},{"$":{"view":"all","id":"p0240"},"#name":"para","_":"Utilize dilated spatial attention and channel attention."}],"$":{"id":"u0015"},"#name":"list-item"},{"$$":[{"#name":"label","_":"•"},{"$":{"view":"all","id":"p0245"},"#name":"para","_":"Use supervision to ease the loss propagation."}],"$":{"id":"u0020"},"#name":"list-item"}],"$":{"id":"l0005"},"#name":"list"}],"$":{"view":"all","id":"sp005"},"#name":"simple-para"}],"$":{"view":"all","id":"as005"},"#name":"abstract-sec"}],"$":{"view":"all","id":"ab005","lang":"en","class":"author-highlights"},"#name":"abstract"},{"$$":[{"$":{"id":"st135"},"#name":"section-title","_":"Abstract"},{"$$":[{"$":{"view":"all","id":"sp010"},"#name":"simple-para","_":"Efficient and accurate semantic segmentation is particularly important in scene understanding for autonomous driving. Although Deep Convolutional Neural Networks(DCNNs) approaches have made a significant improvement for semantic segmentation. However, state-of-the-art models such as Deeplab and PSPNet have complex architectures and high computation complexity. Thus, it is inefficient for realtime applications. On the other hand, many works compromise the performance to obtain real-time inference speed which is critical for developing a light network model with high segmentation accuracy. In this paper, we present a computationally efficient network named DSANet, which follows a two-branch strategy to tackle the problem of real-time semantic segmentation in urban scenes. We first design a Semantic Encoding Branch, which employs channel split and shuffle to reduce the computation and maintain higher segmentation accuracy. Also, we propose a dual attention module consisting of dilated spatial attention and channel attention to make full use of the multi-level feature maps simultaneously, which helps predict the pixel-wise labels in each stage. Meanwhile, Spatial Encoding Network is used to enhance semantic information and preserve the spatial details. To better combine context information and spatial information, we introduce a Simple Feature Fusion Module. We evaluated our model with state-of-the-art semantic image semantic segmentation methods using two challenging datasets. The proposed method achieves an accuracy of 69.9% mean IoU and 71.3% mean IoU at speed of 75.3 fps and 34.08 fps on CamVid and Cityscapes test datasets respectively."}],"$":{"view":"all","id":"as010"},"#name":"abstract-sec"}],"$":{"view":"all","id":"ab010","lang":"en","class":"author"},"#name":"abstract"}],"$":{"xmlns:ce":true,"xmlns:dm":true,"xmlns:sb":true},"#name":"abstracts"}},{"articleTitle":"LMFFNet: A Well-Balanced Lightweight Network for Fast and Accurate Semantic Segmentation","authors":"Shi M., Shen J., Zhou Y.","doi":"10.1109/TNNLS.2022.3176493","externalArticle":true,"openAccess":0,"page":"3205-3219","publicationDate":"1 June 2023","publicationTitle":"IEEE Transactions on Neural Networks and Learning Systems","publicationYear":"2023","scopusArticleUrl":"http://www.scopus.com/scopus/inward/record.url?partnerID=10&rel=3.0.0&view=basic&eid=2-s2.0-85139769643&md5=ccd889cc3ec3ffd364631e7e44d358","scopusEid":"2-s2.0-85139769643","thirdParty":false,"volume":"Volume 34","abstract":{}},{"articleTitle":"MLFNet: Multi-Level Fusion Network for Real-Time Semantic Segmentation of Autonomous Driving","authors":"Fan J., Wang F., Gao B.","doi":"10.1109/TIV.2022.3176860","externalArticle":true,"openAccess":0,"page":"756-767","publicationDate":"1 January 2023","publicationTitle":"IEEE Transactions on Intelligent Vehicles","publicationYear":"2023","scopusArticleUrl":"http://www.scopus.com/scopus/inward/record.url?partnerID=10&rel=3.0.0&view=basic&eid=2-s2.0-85130857356&md5=7ec74a55795acc652b91caff3f8494b7","scopusEid":"2-s2.0-85130857356","thirdParty":false,"volume":"Volume 8","abstract":{}},{"articleTitle":"Joint pyramid attention network for real-time semantic segmentation of urban scenes","authors":"Hu X., Jing L., Sehar U.","doi":"10.1007/s10489-021-02446-8","externalArticle":true,"openAccess":0,"page":"580-594","publicationDate":"January 2022","publicationTitle":"Applied Intelligence","publicationYear":"2022","scopusArticleUrl":"http://www.scopus.com/scopus/inward/record.url?partnerID=10&rel=3.0.0&view=basic&eid=2-s2.0-85